that this file can never drift from CC's official text. The human-readable **Shared-Starter
License deed** is at <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/?deed.en>.

## What the open grant does and does not cover

- **Covered:** your use of the prompt engineering, phase/gate procedures, the question-artifact
  template, the citation-ledger contract, and all original written content in this repository.
- **Attribution (the "BY"):** keep the copyright notice and license notice intact, and state what
  you changed. Credit line: *"Built on the 2A SBA Question-Generator skill by Covie, licensed
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."*
- **ShareAlike (the "SA"):** adaptations, derivative skills, remixes, and any question bank that
  incorporates this material must carry the same CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 license — so a derivative stays
  open and non-commercial too.
- **NonCommercial (the "NC"):** "NonCommercial" means not primarily intended for or directed
  toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. The NC boundary is judged per use, and the
  license's §2(a)(2) preserves anything already allowed by an exception or limitation to copyright
  (e.g. fair use / fair dealing) — those uses sit outside the license and are not restricted by it.
- **Reserved to Covie:** Covie holds the copyright and is **not** bound by the NonCommercial
  limitation against himself. Under §6 of the same license, the licensor may offer the same material
  under **separate (including commercial) terms at any time** without withdrawing the open grant.
  Commercial licensing contact: open an issue on the repository, or reach Covie directly.

## No warranty

The material is provided "as-is", with no warranty of any kind, express or implied. It generates
educational exam-style questions for **FRCR Part 2A revision**. It is **not** medical advice and must
not be used for clinical decisions.

